    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_cb83fbb0641e4ead9008feb4cc6f543249aa48345ab28d9acd5104be29fc8f7e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across the source's analytic and arithmetic representations, the Fourier-support radius acts as a shared budget through distinct concrete mechanisms: compact support annihilates fixed Taylor terms after conversion to Fourier-frequency derivatives near frequency one; on a shifted contour it bounds the off-real-axis growth of the test function and hence the zero-residue error; in the odd prime-power sum it cuts the summation length at a power determined by the support and thereby enters the Jutila and Poisson error exponents; and evaluation at frequency one gates the displayed 1/log X secondary term.",
